IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `nii-il06-nouns`
IMPORT `nii-s65-interpretation`

-- National Insurance Law, s 66 — the right to a child allowance.
-- Quotations (`src:N`) are generated from line N of the deposited source.
--
-- WHAT THIS SECTION DOES. It gives an insured parent a monthly child allowance "for each
-- child", and takes it away from an insured parent who has income chargeable to additional
-- tax within the meaning of s 121B of the Income Tax Ordinance. Which children are "his" for
-- this purpose is s 67 (the count); how much is s 68.
--
-- WHAT IS AN INPUT. Whether the parent has income chargeable to additional tax is decided
-- under the Ordinance, not here (row IL-03 encodes s 121B). Which tax year's income is meant
-- is not said; the input is the caller's answer for the day asked about (fork F5).
--
-- THE EXCLUDED PARENT IS STILL AN INSURED PARENT. The exception is worded "except an insured
-- parent who has …": the parent loses the allowance but remains an insured parent. s 67(b)
-- counts a child with "the insured father", so this row keeps an excluded father in the count
-- he would otherwise have; the child's other parent does not take the child over (fork F6).

§ `Section 66 — right to a child allowance`
-- src:813 | סעיף 66 – זכות לקצבת ילדים [תיקון: תשע״ג־3]
-- src:814 | הורה מבוטח זכאי לקצבת ילדים חודשית לפי פרק זה בעד כל ילד, למעט הורה מבוטח שיש לו הכנסה החייבת במס נוסף כמשמעותה בסעיף 121ב לפקודת מס הכנסה.

-- Version 0.3.0: each rule reads "insured" at the reading of fork F18 its caller passes on
-- (nii-s65-interpretation.l4); the forms by the old names take the reading the switch names. At the
-- declined reading a rule answers what readings (A) and (B) both answer, and is declined where they
-- differ.
@ref National Insurance Law s 66 (source line 814): "למעט הורה מבוטח שיש לו הכנסה החייבת במס נוסף כמשמעותה בסעיף 121ב לפקודת מס הכנסה"
GIVEN `the reading` IS A `A reading of a resident housewife under section 65 "insured" (2)`
      `the person`  IS A `A person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 66 — an insured parent with income chargeable to additional tax, reading a resident housewife as` `the reading` `:` `the person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the reading`
    WHEN `a case that turns on a resident housewife's insurance is declined`
    THEN IF   `at` `a resident housewife is excluded from both limbs` EQUALS `at` `a resident housewife is insured under limb (2)`
         THEN `at` `a resident housewife is excluded from both limbs`
         ELSE `section 65, in limb (2) of the definition of an insured person, does not say whether a resident housewife as defined in section 238, not insured under Chapter 11, is insured under it`
    OTHERWISE `at` `the reading`
    WHERE
        `at` r MEANS
                `s 65 — insured, reading a resident housewife as` r `:` `the person`
            AND `the person`'s `income chargeable to additional tax under section 121B of the Income Tax Ordinance`

@ref National Insurance Law s 66 (source line 814): "הורה מבוטח זכאי לקצבת ילדים חודשית לפי פרק זה בעד כל ילד"
GIVEN `the reading` IS A `A reading of a resident housewife under section 65 "insured" (2)`
      `the person`  IS A `A person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 66 — entitled to a monthly child allowance for each child in the count, reading a resident housewife as` `the reading` `:` `the person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the reading`
    WHEN `a case that turns on a resident housewife's insurance is declined`
    THEN IF   `at` `a resident housewife is excluded from both limbs` EQUALS `at` `a resident housewife is insured under limb (2)`
         THEN `at` `a resident housewife is excluded from both limbs`
         ELSE `section 65, in limb (2) of the definition of an insured person, does not say whether a resident housewife as defined in section 238, not insured under Chapter 11, is insured under it`
    OTHERWISE `at` `the reading`
    WHERE
        `at` r MEANS
                `s 65 — insured, reading a resident housewife as` r `:` `the person`
            AND NOT `s 66 — an insured parent with income chargeable to additional tax, reading a resident housewife as` r `:` `the person`

